The schema shows that `agents.list` is an array of agent objects. Each agent can have its own `models` catalog. Also note the `defaults` section is separate.

Given our config already has `defaults` with models. The `list` array is currently missing (we haven't successfully added one). We need to add a `list` entry with at least one agent (`nvidia`). But maybe we can instead set `agents.list` to an array containing the `nvidia` agent, while leaving `defaults` untouched.

Let's construct a valid patch:

{
  "agents": {
    "list": [
      {
        "id": "nvidia",
        "model": { "primary": "openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free" },
        "models": {
          "openrouter/auto": { "alias": "OpenRouter" },
          "openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free": {},
          "moonshotai/kimi-k2.5": { "alias": "Kimi K2.5" },
          "stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash": { "alias": "Step-3.5-Flash" },
          "z-ai/glm4.7": { "alias": "GLM-4.7" },
          "nvidia/moonshotai/kimi-k2.5": { "alias": "Kimi K2.5 (NVIDIA)" },
          "nvidia/stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash": { "alias": "Step-3.5-Flash (NVIDIA)" },
          "nvidia/z-ai/glm4.7": { "alias": "GLM-4.7 (NVIDIA)" }
        },
        "workspace": "/root/.openclaw/workspace",
        "maxConcurrent": 4,
        "subagents": { "maxConcurrent": 8 }
      }
    ]
